course: dictionary
lesson: 16097
title: A waxwork is a wax model
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A waxwork is a life-size model of a person, made of wax. Wax is the soft material candles are made from. «Lily stared at the waxwork of the queen, and it looked almost real.» The clue is that it is a model of a person, not the person.
explain: Look at the words around it to find the meaning. «We took the train to London to visit the waxworks.» Visit tells you the waxworks is a place, a museum full of models. Ask yourself: is this one model, or a whole place? The s at the end often means the place.
explain: Words can also make you feel something. «In the dark hall, the waxwork figures looked so real that Sam felt a little spooky.» Spooky is the feeling, and it comes from how lifelike the figures look. Always test your meaning by putting it into the sentence and checking that it still makes sense.
fact: A waxwork is a life-size model of a person, made of wax.
fact: «Waxwork» usually means one model, often of a famous person.
fact: «Waxworks» can also mean a museum or exhibition of such models, such as Madame Tussauds in London.
fact: Waxworks can feel spooky in stories, because the figures look almost alive.
fact: A clue like visit or looked tells you whether waxworks means one model or the whole museum.
exercise: «Dad took us to see a waxwork of the king.» What is a waxwork? | A type of candle used at birthdays | A painting hung on a wall | *A life-size model of a person made of wax | A real king who lives in a palace
exercise: «We spent the whole day at the waxworks in London.» What does waxworks mean here? | A busy railway station | A shop that sells candles | A long, dark tunnel | *A museum full of wax models of famous people
exercise: In «The waxwork looked so real that Mia nearly said hello», what does looked so real show? | It is a real person standing very still | It is a painting on the wall | It can talk and walk around the room | *It looks like a real person, but it is only a model
test: Which sentence uses waxwork correctly? | *«A waxwork of the singer stood in the museum.» | «We baked a waxwork in the oven.» | «She wrote a waxwork in her diary.» | «The waxwork ran fast around the park.»
test: In «We queued for an hour at the waxworks», what does waxworks mean? | A long queue for ice cream | A type of tall tree | *A place where wax models are on show | A school for artists
exam: Priya says a waxwork is a real person who stands still in a shop. What is a waxwork? | A type of statue made of stone | *A life-size model made of wax | A real person who is very tired | A kind of cake
